<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="af-sequences">
  <title>Sequences</title>

  <objectives>
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <ul>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-17" /> — Linear patterns</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-18" /> — Arithmetic sequences — nth term</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-af-19" /> — Quadratic and geometric sequences (HL)</li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <p>
    A <term>sequence</term> is an ordered list of numbers following a rule.
    An <term>arithmetic sequence</term> has a constant difference <m>d</m> between consecutive terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <term>nth term</term> (general term) of an arithmetic sequence: <m>T_n = a + (n-1)d</m>
    where <m>a</m> is the first term and <m>d</m> is the common difference.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Example:</strong> The sequence <m>3, 7, 11, 15, \ldots</m> has <m>a = 3</m>, <m>d = 4</m>.
    So <m>T_n = 3 + (n-1)(4) = 4n - 1</m>.
  </p>
  <p>
    A <term>geometric sequence</term> (HL) has a constant ratio <m>r</m>: <m>T_n = ar^{n-1}</m>.
  </p>

  <exercises xml:id="exs-sequences">
    <title>Exercises</title>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-sequence-nth-term">
      <statement><p>Find the nth term of the sequence: <m>5, 9, 13, 17, \ldots</m></p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>T_n = 4n + 1</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>a = 5</m>, <m>d = 4</m>. <m>T_n = 5 + (n-1)(4) = 5 + 4n - 4 = 4n + 1</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-sequence-term-value">
      <statement><p>For the sequence with <m>T_n = 3n - 2</m>, find the 20th term and find which term equals 55.</p></statement>
      <answer><p>20th term: 58; the 19th term equals 55.</p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>T_{20} = 3(20) - 2 = 58</m>. For <m>3n - 2 = 55</m>: <m>3n = 57</m>, <m>n = 19</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

  </exercises>

</section>
